## Request

Extend the existing schema-3 recursive-closure proof contract with the smallest hooks-only
risk-adaptive verification increment. Reuse declaration and result JSON rather than adding a new
authority table. Keep prior M1 through M3B evidence as history and preserve the already-open Work3
and Work5 boundaries.

## Required Behavior

- Define canonical `mechanical`, `normal`, and `high-risk` profiles and a versioned policy digest.
- Classify explicit changed paths/components, declared side effects, target class, and protected
  boundary inputs deterministically.
- Treat parent minimums as floors, compose mixed changes at the highest applicable profile, and
  escalate unknown or unexpected scope.
- Bind recipe identity and proof-attempt idempotency to the effective profile and policy digest.
- Retain classification reasons, required recipe set, and escalation history in immutable proof
  evidence.
- Keep automatic lowering disabled. A caller may request or explain a profile, but cannot obtain a
  shallower effective profile than the governing safe default, parent floor, or protected floor.

## Development Boundary

Only the canonical source and known split development targets are in scope. Preserve unrelated
App Server edits in the canonical worktree. Do not push, publish, migrate or deploy production,
alter credentials, close Work3/Work5, or claim measured token savings.

## Verification

- Focused unit tests cover each profile, mixed composition, parent/protected floors, unknown and
  unexpected-scope escalation, immutable policy identity, proof-attempt binding, and disabled
  automatic lowering.
- The exact committed snapshot is installed and exercised on the disposable Linux and Windows
  test beds.
- Hosted-development health remains green; update it only if the changed behavior reaches that
  surface.
- Record durable Work2 evidence and register the exact candidate with the open CAMP → PRM → MAP →
  Idea outcome chain.
